{# ===========================================================================
   SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the site navigation menu.

   Every page (both the .site-nav grid family AND the self-contained .topbar
   "vector" family) includes this partial in place of a hand-copied
   <div class="nav-links"> block, so the menu can never drift between pages
   again. The surrounding chrome (the <nav>/<div class="topbar"> wrapper, the
   search box, the theme/lang controls) stays per-page; only the link list is
   shared.

   • Self-contained t() macro — so it works whether or not the host page
     defines its own (an {% include %} does not import the parent's macros).
   • nav_prefix — optional. Pages rendered one directory deep (site/sectors/*)
     set {% set nav_prefix = '../' %} before including so every link resolves
     from the site root (a bare href="macro.html" would 404 as /sectors/...).
   • No per-page `active` class — theme.js highlights the current page (and its
     parent dropdown) by matching the URL, so highlighting stays consistent.

   Structure: Home · United States · China · Hong Kong · Canada · International ·
   Other Assets (3-tier: Bitcoin Vector ▸ / Commodities ▸ fly out; Forex, Bonds
   are leaves) · Research.
   =========================================================================== #}
